        {label:"Described figure &mdash; hormone levels across the cycle (Fig. D3.1.7)", text:"Plotted against the 28-day cycle, FSH rises gently as follicles develop, then both FSH and (more sharply) LH surge around day 13&ndash;14, coinciding with ovulation; oestradiol rises steadily to a peak just before day 14 then falls, while progesterone rises after ovulation to a broad peak (secreted by the corpus luteum) before falling toward day 28 if fertilization has not occurred."}
