        "From about seven days after conception, the blastocyst (and later the placenta alone) secretes hCG (human chorionic gonadotropin), which appears in the urine and maintains the corpus luteum &mdash; and so progesterone secretion &mdash; for at least the first 16 weeks of pregnancy; this is the hormone detected by home pregnancy tests.",
